1: // Sub-agent sessions out of the user's resume list.
2: //
3: // spawn_agents children are headless agent runs with session files of
4: // their own. Up to 0.9.0 they were written next to the user's sessions
5: // (<agentDir>/sessions/<cwd-slug>/), so the core's session picker
6: // (/resume) listed every sub-agent run and --continue picked whichever
7: // session file changed last — often a background sub-agent's rather than
8: // the user's conversation. Children now go to <session dir>/subagents/
9: // (agents-lib.ts subagentSessionDir), which the core never lists.
10: //
11: // moveLegacySubagentSessions puts the children older releases left in a
12: // session dir into that folder too (moved, never deleted: the session uploader
13: // still finds them there when a resumed session records its sub-agents).
14: // It runs at every agent launch before the core picks a session, and
15: // stays cheap on large folders: a marker per session dir records when it
16: // was last sorted, and only files changed since then are opened (their
17: // first lines only). Files changed in the last minute are left for the
18: // next launch, in case an older release is still writing them.
19: //
20: // A child is recognised from the top of its session file, by the same
21: // signals the session uploader uses (engine-messages.ts subagentTask): the marker entry
22: // a sub-agent writes into its own session before its task
23: // (SUBAGENT_ENTRY_TYPE), or — sessions of releases that wrote no marker —
24: // a first user message "Task: <task>" (SUBAGENT_TASK_PREFIX), confirmed by
25: // the role prompt every sub-agent has run with since 0.5.4 (appended to
26: // the system prompt: "You are a <role> subagent ..."), which the file
27: // itself carries, so no other session has to be read.
